      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We examined the expression of preproenkephalin mRNA in pain-modulating regions of the rat's brainstem using in situ hybridization histochemistry. We found that neurones in the Kölliker-Fuse nucleus, which receives projections from spinal nociceptive-specific cells, express enkephalin mRNA, that this expression is increased by noxious pinch applied to the skin of awake animals, and that these enkephalinergic neurones are part of a descending system that terminates in the rostroventral medulla and the spinal cord. These findings show that natural noxious stimuli activate opioidergic bulbospinal neurones that could directly modulate spinal nociceptive transmission."},
